WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.000
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.040
tablets each

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.640
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night

5
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.760
before your procedure.

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.560
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

7
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.640
ounces of water

8
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:30.270
up to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water,

9
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.040
finishing all

10
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.120
12 tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

11
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.620
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

12
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.320
of water

13
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.770
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes

14
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.560
after finishing

15
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.470
that container. Fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the

16
00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.880
entire amount over 30

17
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:04.340
minutes. That completes your first dose. 7 hours prior to your procedure,

18
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.280
repeat the exact

19
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.730
same three steps using your second bottle of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2

20
00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.160
minutes with water,

21
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.390
then 16 ounces of water one hour later, then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes

22
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.320
after that.

23
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.320
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

24
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.560
directed, even if

25
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.450
you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough, but

26
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:30.800
finishing the entire dose

27
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.820
is what gives us the clearest view during your procedure. If the prep isn't

28
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.240
completed as directed,

29
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.100
we may need to reschedule and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep

30
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.440
drinking clear

31
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.190
liquids to stay hydrated. It will help you feel better and help the prep do its

32
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:45.600
job.

33
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:50.840
Do not drink anything at all within 4 hours of your procedure, including

34
00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.200
water,

35
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.490
unless it is a small sip to take a medication. Your procedure may be canceled

36
00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.720
or rescheduled

37
00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.280
if this is not followed. If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips

38
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.320
to the bathroom,

39
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.480
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

40
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:12.560
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

41
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.160
hydrated. If you have

42
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.370
any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here to

43
00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:18.680
help.
